Jim, I'm afraid something's gone wrong. What do you think?

00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:11.290
Control calling a starting. Control calling a starting.

00:22:12.050 --> 00:22:13.740
Are you receiving me? Over.

00:22:14.840 --> 00:22:17.240
A starting to control. Receiving you loud and clear. Over.

00:22:17.890 --> 00:22:21.570
Jim, you're the control gears, dammit. We're working on it now.

00:22:22.220 --> 00:22:23.860
But until it's fixed, you're on your own.

00:22:24.370 --> 00:22:26.090
Yes, but you'll have to tell me what to do.

00:22:26.610 --> 00:22:29.780
Good. Now, Jim, move over into the pilot's seat.

00:22:30.350 --> 00:22:31.710
And let Pat take over the transmitter.

00:22:31.970 --> 00:22:33.570
The radar is useless. They're out of range.

00:22:33.900 --> 00:22:35.660
Get on to Jotelbank. Don't start tracking.

00:22:38.840 --> 00:22:40.780
Connect me to Jotelbank fast. This is an emergency.

00:22:43.880 --> 00:22:45.200
Hello, Dad. Jim's all ready.

00:22:45.830 --> 00:22:48.820
All right. Now, at the left, top of the console,

00:22:49.700 --> 00:22:51.500
there's the blast chamber temperature gauge.

00:22:52.160 --> 00:22:52.780
Give me the reading.

00:22:53.210 --> 00:22:55.070
Wait a minute. I've got it.

00:22:55.250 --> 00:22:56.370
It's nearly a danger mark.

00:22:56.640 --> 00:22:57.960
It's nearly a danger mark.

00:22:58.750 --> 00:22:59.510
Danger mark?

00:23:00.700 --> 00:23:04.500
overheating they're still going at blast-off power but they'll explode or burn up they can't

00:23:04.500 --> 00:23:11.510
last long at that heat no no pat how much fuel have you used the needle's flickering on the

00:23:11.510 --> 00:23:16.040
three-quarter mark then you're burning too much fuel you're still going at full power we've got

00:23:16.040 --> 00:23:22.410
to catch your speed move the throttle lever to close the fuel jets that's the lever to jim's left

00:23:22.410 --> 00:23:24.900
move it slowly to a half

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:30.240
Halfway.

00:23:31.040 --> 00:23:31.400
Halfway.

00:23:32.430 --> 00:23:33.670
Move it slowly back to a quarter.

00:23:34.080 --> 00:23:34.920
It won't be enough.

00:23:35.340 --> 00:23:36.000
I know that, Joe.

00:23:36.600 --> 00:23:37.780
They'll have to use their retro rockets.

00:23:38.100 --> 00:23:39.680
In those seats, it could break their necks.

00:23:39.840 --> 00:23:40.920
But it's our only chance.

00:23:41.770 --> 00:23:45.440
Pat, tell Jim you've got to use the retro rockets to counteract your speed.

00:23:45.870 --> 00:23:47.330
Look for the ignition speed.

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:48.600
It's plenty marked.

00:23:50.730 --> 00:23:51.230
Now, wait a minute.

00:23:51.790 --> 00:23:52.870
Don't touch it until I tell you.

00:23:53.860 --> 00:23:54.680
Are you both strapped in?

00:23:55.370 --> 00:23:55.670
Yes.

00:23:56.600 --> 00:23:56.740
Good.

00:23:57.540 --> 00:23:59.060
Underneath, you'll find the firing button.

00:24:00.030 --> 00:24:04.380
switch on the ignition and a red light will appear when you get the red light

00:24:04.380 --> 00:24:12.080
press the button have you got that yes right ready now this will reduce your

00:24:12.080 --> 00:24:16.480
speed ignition on now all red lights will be shown

00:24:16.660 --> 00:24:25.520
nothing's happened nothing's happened all right don't worry maybe it's a fault

00:24:25.520 --> 00:24:28.160
on the light bulb press the firing button

00:24:30.030 --> 00:24:33.870
Loud swish and feel a sudden breaking motion as the retros go to action.

00:24:35.280 --> 00:24:37.780
When you're ready, fire!

00:24:39.660 --> 00:24:41.660
It's not working, Dad! It's not working!

00:24:41.860 --> 00:24:43.320
There must be a fault on the circuit!

00:24:43.860 --> 00:24:44.560
What should we do?

00:24:46.280 --> 00:24:47.320
Dad! Dad!

00:24:48.660 --> 00:24:49.940
Things wrong, he's not answering!

00:24:51.420 --> 00:24:52.580
It's starting calling control.

00:24:53.010 --> 00:24:54.270
It's starting calling control.

00:24:54.730 --> 00:24:55.450
Come in, please.

00:24:55.770 --> 00:24:56.790
Come in, please, control.

00:25:01.690 --> 00:25:04.060
We've lost them. It must be the rotation of the Earth, Doctor.

00:25:04.180 --> 00:25:05.080
They've gone beyond our field.

00:25:05.220 --> 00:25:09.760
It's going up, Cape Canaveral, and Womora-2, and all radio telescopes.

00:25:10.380 --> 00:25:13.320
Tell them to start tracking. We'll arrange radio links.

00:25:13.700 --> 00:25:14.600
How long's that going to be?

00:25:14.960 --> 00:25:15.840
Hard to tell yet, sir.

00:25:16.060 --> 00:25:18.380
Well, you heard the retro rockets didn't work.

00:25:18.540 --> 00:25:21.080
They're hurtling throughout the space, completely out of control.

00:25:22.660 --> 00:25:23.560
He's still in a deep coma.

00:25:24.620 --> 00:25:26.320
Two fellas in the rocket are probably in the same state.

00:25:27.750 --> 00:25:29.530
If you could find some way of snapping him out of it.

00:25:30.090 --> 00:25:32.530
We could tell the children they could try the same on Peter and Mike.

00:25:32.780 --> 00:25:34.880
Well, if only we knew what sort of weapon would cause the damage.

00:25:35.540 --> 00:25:36.240
This was the weapon.

00:25:37.610 --> 00:25:38.110
Dr. Valentine?

00:25:38.980 --> 00:25:40.260
Colonel Armstrong, Special Intelligence.

00:25:40.830 --> 00:25:41.910
Have you ever seen anything like this before?

00:25:42.130 --> 00:25:44.140
Not have I.

00:25:45.120 --> 00:25:46.020
Just what did it do?

00:25:46.160 --> 00:25:50.340
There was a flash and a high-pitched sort of whining noise.

00:25:51.150 --> 00:25:52.350
A wind assault on eyes and ears.

00:25:53.690 --> 00:25:55.090
Now, that could mean the brain was overstimulated,

00:25:55.350 --> 00:25:56.710
and that would cause this sort of breakdown.

00:25:57.520 --> 00:25:59.440
I'll get this examined by experts to see where it comes from.

00:26:00.380 --> 00:26:02.440
Some foreign power is trying to stop us reaching Venus.

00:26:02.840 --> 00:26:04.840
We've got to discover why before it's too late.

00:26:10.260 --> 00:26:11.000
Calling us starting.

00:26:11.240 --> 00:26:13.430
Dad, wake up.

00:26:13.510 --> 00:26:14.410
Lily's coming over the radio.

00:26:14.680 --> 00:26:15.440
Calling us starting.

00:26:15.780 --> 00:26:17.200
Cape Canaveral calling us starting.

00:26:17.500 --> 00:26:18.660
Come and please, Venus rocket.

00:26:19.190 --> 00:26:20.570
Hello, it's starting to Cape Canaveral.

00:26:20.630 --> 00:26:21.510
Are we glad to hear you?

00:26:21.850 --> 00:26:23.410
We've got to hook up with our starting control.

00:26:24.080 --> 00:26:24.840
Go ahead, England.

00:26:25.850 --> 00:26:26.390
Hello, Pat.

00:26:27.230 --> 00:26:28.230
You and Jimson all right?

00:26:28.760 --> 00:26:29.380
Yes, Dad.

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:30.720
What about Mike and Peter?

00:26:31.240 --> 00:26:31.900
Still unconscious.

00:26:32.640 --> 00:26:33.680
Well, don't lose hope.

00:26:34.170 --> 00:26:36.830
We'll soon have the auto control gear working again and bring you down.

00:26:37.480 --> 00:26:38.140
Now, don't worry.

00:26:38.560 --> 00:26:39.880
I'll call you next through Woomera.

00:26:43.830 --> 00:26:44.470
Can you see anything?

00:26:44.690 --> 00:26:45.790
Just a tiny speck.

00:26:46.030 --> 00:26:47.010
It might be Earth.

00:26:47.200 --> 00:26:48.520
It's too small to recognize.

00:26:49.910 --> 00:26:53.710
Jim, suppose Dad can't get us back?

00:26:53.850 --> 00:26:54.350
He will.

00:26:54.630 --> 00:26:55.450
Oh, don't pretend.

00:26:55.870 --> 00:26:57.740
I know we'll soon be beyond his reach.

00:26:58.860 --> 00:26:59.180
Then.

00:27:00.220 --> 00:27:02.000
Well, we'll just go on and on and on, I suppose.

00:27:03.000 --> 00:27:04.340
Until the fuel runs out.

00:27:04.890 --> 00:27:06.070
Well, that doesn't make any difference.

00:27:06.470 --> 00:27:08.310
You see, there's no atmosphere in space to stop us.

00:27:08.310 --> 00:27:09.150
No gravity, nothing.

00:27:09.810 --> 00:27:12.790
So we'll just go on and on into nothingness forever.

00:27:14.340 --> 00:27:15.360
Jim, I'm scared.

00:27:15.960 --> 00:27:16.640
So am I.

00:27:24.460 --> 00:27:26.510
Doctor, we're getting something.

00:27:27.190 --> 00:27:27.870
Be quiet.

00:27:29.550 --> 00:27:29.970
We're getting a doctor.

00:27:30.380 --> 00:27:37.330
The calculations were right. I was hoping I'd made a mistake.

00:27:38.160 --> 00:27:39.980
In a few minutes, they'll be completely out of our control.

00:27:40.080 --> 00:27:42.640
Oh, no, they won't, sir. It's working again.

00:27:43.360 --> 00:27:44.100
Try it and save.

00:27:46.330 --> 00:27:48.370
They seem to have been going an awful long time.

00:27:48.740 --> 00:27:51.170
Time? Time doesn't mean anything anymore.

00:27:51.950 --> 00:27:52.310
Look!

00:27:52.590 --> 00:27:59.880
Your control! Dad must have control, he must have!

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:03.560
He's got us. He's got us. Jim, we're not going to die after all.

00:28:05.060 --> 00:28:06.580
Just getting him on the Woomera link, Doctor.

00:28:08.810 --> 00:28:12.130
Hello, Woomera. This is a starty rocket receiving you loud and clear. Over.

00:28:12.430 --> 00:28:15.870
Fine. We'll link you up with a starty base control now.

00:28:16.150 --> 00:28:17.190
Come in, Doctor Valentine.

00:28:17.790 --> 00:28:20.640
Hello, Pat and Jim. The order control is working again.

00:28:21.020 --> 00:28:23.260
I'm going to try and fire your retros from here.

00:28:23.750 --> 00:28:26.330
Make sure you're stuck in your seats. Do you understand?

00:28:26.760 --> 00:28:27.580
We're all set, Dad.

00:28:28.470 --> 00:28:29.980
Good. Stand by.

00:28:30.030 --> 00:28:53.100
I will fire him. Now. Good. It worked. According to my controls, your speed is coming down. Are you all right? Pat, Jim, are you all right? Pat, Jim, are you receiving me? Pat, Jim, are you receiving me?

00:28:53.750 --> 00:28:59.280
Yes, we're still here. It worked. I knew he would.

00:29:01.180 --> 00:29:05.220
Good. Now I'm going to try and alter your course to bring you back into orbit.

00:29:06.870 --> 00:29:10.240
Fantastic. Orbiting the Earth at such a distance. Let's hope we can hold them.

00:29:11.210 --> 00:29:12.070
How do you mean hold them?

00:29:12.700 --> 00:29:16.180
Well, at such a speed, the rocket wants to go streaking away. It's only the order control.

00:29:16.300 --> 00:29:20.260
Core in control. Core in control. We're picking up something on the radar.

00:29:25.280 --> 00:29:28.120
White darts. Like a snowstorm.

00:29:30.280 --> 00:29:33.790
They're getting bigger. They're coming straight for us.

00:29:34.690 --> 00:29:35.090
Meteor.

00:29:36.310 --> 00:29:38.030
Give me the bearing, Pat. We'll try to dodge them.

00:29:39.510 --> 00:29:40.350
Three, seven.

00:29:50.370 --> 00:29:53.900
Meteor shot. Broken. I'll contact with the rocket.

00:29:55.560 --> 00:29:56.060
It's no good.

00:29:57.920 --> 00:29:58.300
Blossom.

00:29:59.640 --> 00:29:59.980
Pandora.

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:02.500
Mr. Valentine regained control of the runaway rocket.

00:30:03.990 --> 00:30:06.210
Come next week and see episode three,

00:30:06.980 --> 00:30:08.560
The Men with Six Fingers.

00:30:09.440 --> 00:30:28.670
Got into space by the saboteurs,

00:30:29.200 --> 00:30:29.780
Pat and Jim.

00:30:30.090 --> 00:30:33.340
with Mike and Pete unconscious, soar into space.

00:30:33.620 --> 00:30:36.890
Dr. Ballantyne manages to regain control of the rocket,

00:30:37.790 --> 00:30:41.880
but Astarte runs into a meteor shower and the doctor loses contact.

00:31:01.470 --> 00:31:03.070
Astartic can't take this beating for long.

00:31:03.620 --> 00:31:05.500
If one of those meteors pierces the skin...

00:31:08.310 --> 00:31:10.030
Oh, for you, sir.

00:31:18.550 --> 00:31:19.470
This is Dr. Wilson here.

00:31:20.120 --> 00:31:21.920
Your radar operator. He's recovered consciousness.

00:31:22.480 --> 00:31:24.320
There don't seem to be any harmful after effects.

00:31:24.980 --> 00:31:25.620
Good, thanks.

00:31:25.820 --> 00:31:27.540
Look, I can't talk now. I'll call you back later.

00:31:31.340 --> 00:31:38.070
Yes, Donald Bank, yes, we're in direct contact, but they seem to have run into a cloud of meteors, and we've lost them.

00:31:38.590 --> 00:31:39.410
Just keep tracking, please.

00:31:54.360 --> 00:31:59.890
Finding Flash, there's noise inside my head that's the kids.

00:32:00.060 --> 00:32:03.280
Pat and Jim, how did we get into the cabin?

00:32:03.620 --> 00:32:05.060
What's that noise?

00:32:05.700 --> 00:32:06.160
It's the method.

00:32:07.720 --> 00:32:09.640
Mike, we're in outer space.

00:32:09.860 --> 00:32:10.020
What?

00:32:11.300 --> 00:32:12.080
Here, Pat, Jim.

00:32:12.840 --> 00:32:14.560
Mike, Peter, you're all right.

00:32:15.060 --> 00:32:16.460
Pat, Pat, wake up.

00:32:16.540 --> 00:32:17.780
Look, Peter and Mike have come round.

00:32:23.770 --> 00:32:24.580
Right, thank you.

00:32:25.370 --> 00:32:26.290
I've got those ghost figures.

00:32:27.180 --> 00:32:28.600
You'll give me a ring if there's any change.

00:32:29.860 --> 00:32:29.960
Thanks.

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:35.400
You're still tracking.

00:32:36.090 --> 00:32:37.490
She got through the meteor shower, right?

00:32:37.870 --> 00:32:38.410
That's something.

00:32:38.610 --> 00:32:39.150
I suppose so.

00:32:39.430 --> 00:32:40.210
Any luck with the radio?

00:32:40.680 --> 00:32:41.540
Nothing yet, I'm afraid.

00:32:42.640 --> 00:32:45.700
And the only way we could save Astarte from blowing up was to blast off.

00:32:45.910 --> 00:32:48.710
And with the autocontrol damaged and you two unconscious,

00:32:49.010 --> 00:32:51.030
we weren't able to get it under proper control.

00:32:51.400 --> 00:32:52.880
I think they've done wonderfully, don't you, Mike?

00:32:53.180 --> 00:32:54.040
I certainly do.

00:32:54.820 --> 00:32:56.040
Well, we'll soon get the place, Shipshet.

00:33:00.670 --> 00:33:02.370
You haven't switched on the artificial gravity.

00:33:02.990 --> 00:33:04.840
Well, I'm sorry, I didn't realise.

00:33:05.000 --> 00:33:06.360
We haven't been out of our seats for hours.

00:33:06.560 --> 00:33:09.560
I swear it's only under my seat or I'll be floating around this cabin like a balloon.

00:33:14.450 --> 00:33:16.950
There's been a bit of electrical damage, but I think I can fix it.

00:33:17.090 --> 00:33:20.180
Good. Well, I'd better try and find out where on earth we are.

00:33:20.480 --> 00:33:21.820
Don't you mean where in space?

00:33:22.670 --> 00:33:25.170
I suppose I do, really. I'll go and make some calculations.

00:33:28.400 --> 00:33:29.420
I think I'll look at the scenery.

00:33:32.170 --> 00:33:36.690
Oh, it's beautiful. The stars like huge diamonds on black velvet.

00:33:37.310 --> 00:33:37.750
Hey, Pete.

00:33:38.450 --> 00:33:38.610
Yeah?

00:33:39.550 --> 00:33:41.450
I found out what's wrong with the retro rotters.

00:33:41.820 --> 00:33:44.800
Those two, when they bashed up the remote control, blew our main fuse.

00:33:45.000 --> 00:33:45.440
Can you fix it?

00:33:45.600 --> 00:33:46.020
Leave it to me.

00:33:46.280 --> 00:33:46.440
Good.

00:33:47.120 --> 00:33:49.260
Well, you'll be pleased to know I've plotted our exact position.

00:33:49.610 --> 00:33:51.970
Pat, you should be seeing Venus out of that port any moment.

00:33:52.630 --> 00:33:53.950
Not that that matters, of course, now.

00:34:01.880 --> 00:34:02.120
Anything?

00:34:02.760 --> 00:34:03.300
Afraid not.

00:34:03.720 --> 00:34:06.120
Joddle banks say they're still tracking, but Astarte isn't answering.

00:34:06.710 --> 00:34:08.350
There's been nothing since they ran into the meteors.

00:34:08.570 --> 00:34:10.190
They may have put the radio out of action.

00:34:10.920 --> 00:34:12.500
Look, why don't you try and get some rest, Doctor?

00:34:12.620 --> 00:34:14.620
I'm all right now, and if we get any news, I'll let you know.

00:34:14.820 --> 00:34:16.360
I couldn't sleep, George. I'll hang on here.

00:34:17.060 --> 00:34:18.220
I see you're still on auto-control.

00:34:18.800 --> 00:34:19.940
Yes, but it's dead.

00:34:20.800 --> 00:34:22.000
Your aerials must be damaged.

00:34:22.450 --> 00:34:24.030
We've absolutely no control from here.

00:34:28.110 --> 00:34:28.790
Starte control?

00:34:29.420 --> 00:34:29.740
Yes.

00:34:30.190 --> 00:34:32.160
Yes, they have.

00:34:33.200 --> 00:34:36.080
Thanks, Federal Bank.

00:34:36.880 --> 00:34:38.100
Astarte's changing course.

00:34:38.460 --> 00:34:38.700
What?

00:34:38.920 --> 00:34:40.610
They must be on live control.

00:34:41.360 --> 00:34:41.760
Try the lever.

00:34:43.800 --> 00:34:45.310
Yes, they're all right.

00:34:46.950 --> 00:34:48.010
Astarte calling control.

00:34:48.490 --> 00:34:49.630
Astarte calling control.

00:34:50.120 --> 00:34:50.760
Come in, please.

00:34:51.040 --> 00:34:51.680
Come in, please.

00:34:52.750 --> 00:34:53.510
They're not answering.

00:34:53.830 --> 00:34:54.670
Oh, give them time.

00:34:55.060 --> 00:34:55.740
Time what for?

00:34:55.920 --> 00:34:57.480
Have you forgotten the speed of radio waves?

00:34:57.600 --> 00:34:59.160
They're fast, I know, but we're a long way up.

00:34:59.530 --> 00:34:59.970
Of course I...

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:00.420
I'm an idiot.

00:35:03.210 --> 00:35:03.750
Is it?

00:35:04.630 --> 00:35:05.770
Started calling control.

00:35:06.300 --> 00:35:07.380
Started calling control.

00:35:08.580 --> 00:35:08.920
Jim!

00:35:09.410 --> 00:35:09.950
That's wonderful.

00:35:10.270 --> 00:35:10.710
Are you alright?

00:35:13.650 --> 00:35:18.110
Space rock designers, two children aboard, once again under control.

00:35:19.080 --> 00:35:23.840
Pilot and engineer of both recovered consciousness with apparently no after effects have resumed

00:35:23.840 --> 00:35:24.720
their normal duty.

00:35:28.250 --> 00:35:28.910
Ballantyne here.

00:35:30.220 --> 00:35:30.460
Who?

00:35:31.740 --> 00:35:32.340
Downing Street.

00:35:33.830 --> 00:35:34.370
Yes, put them on.

00:35:37.230 --> 00:35:38.030
Good evening, Prime Minister.

00:35:39.860 --> 00:35:41.020
Yes, of course I'm relieved.

00:35:43.740 --> 00:35:45.200
Yes, I suppose they could.

00:35:45.460 --> 00:35:47.880
You want what?

00:35:49.520 --> 00:35:50.860
You know, I wish we were going on to Venus.

00:35:51.160 --> 00:35:52.800
Haven't you had enough excitement for one trip?

00:35:52.980 --> 00:35:55.060
It seems a pity to turn back now we've come so far.

00:35:55.280 --> 00:35:56.940
We can hardly go on without a proper crew.

00:35:57.270 --> 00:35:58.130
I like that.

00:35:59.270 --> 00:35:59.970
No, there aren't...

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:02.500
The two astronauts in the business I'd rather travel with than Pat and Jim.

00:36:02.620 --> 00:36:04.920
If we aren't careful, we'll be out of a jog.

00:36:05.880 --> 00:36:08.320
Still, my first duty to your father is to get you back safe and sound.

00:36:09.070 --> 00:36:11.070
Venus has waited a long time for a visit from Earth.

00:36:11.700 --> 00:36:12.440
Can wait a bit longer.

00:36:19.200 --> 00:36:19.880
Call him up again?

00:36:20.240 --> 00:36:21.100
Another five minutes.

00:36:22.280 --> 00:36:23.260
You're supposed to be in bed, sir.

00:36:23.420 --> 00:36:23.880
Is something wrong?

00:36:24.350 --> 00:36:25.980
Yes, in a way.

00:36:26.900 --> 00:36:28.120
I've just had a call from the government.

