00:55:01.660 --> 00:55:03.790
You may lose contact for a while.

00:55:04.190 --> 00:55:05.170
I'm going down.

00:55:05.860 --> 00:55:07.160
The machine's pulling like mad.

00:55:07.620 --> 00:55:08.160
Don't worry.

00:55:08.460 --> 00:55:09.300
I've got the rope.

00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:58.370
You are calling Astarte. You're receiving me. Come in Astarte.

00:55:58.630 --> 00:55:59.190
Thank heavens.

00:56:02.080 --> 00:56:06.420
Astarte calling control. Astarte calling control. Yes, we are receiving you.

00:56:06.540 --> 00:56:18.110
What is that kind of super magnet? A sort of gravity machine?

00:56:18.290 --> 00:56:20.150
Well, that's what's been interfering with our radio.

00:56:20.620 --> 00:56:21.560
Yes, could be.

00:56:21.950 --> 00:56:24.470
Hello, Astarte. You are all in great danger.

00:56:25.050 --> 00:56:26.770
There are men on Venus and they're hostile.

00:56:27.840 --> 00:56:29.980
One thing's certain. Whoever made that thing technically...

00:56:30.030 --> 00:56:31.390
Okay, they're centuries ahead of us.

00:56:31.600 --> 00:56:32.600
Calling the Earthmen.

00:56:32.880 --> 00:56:33.720
Calling the Earthmen.

00:56:34.150 --> 00:56:35.650
Be clear and understand.

00:56:36.770 --> 00:56:37.930
Receiving you loud and clear.

00:56:38.130 --> 00:56:38.610
Who are you?

00:56:38.920 --> 00:56:40.080
I am master of Venus.

00:56:40.690 --> 00:56:41.710
Come in peace or war?

00:56:41.930 --> 00:56:42.470
In peace.

00:56:42.870 --> 00:56:43.590
We come as friends.

00:56:44.160 --> 00:56:47.860
If you come in peace, follow the light to the end of the tunnel, and we shall see if

00:56:47.860 --> 00:56:48.640
you speak the truth.

00:56:49.450 --> 00:56:50.130
It may be a trap.

00:56:50.840 --> 00:56:51.660
Suppose we refuse.

00:56:51.920 --> 00:56:53.980
If you refuse, we shall assume you come in war.

00:56:54.300 --> 00:56:57.980
Your rocket will be destroyed as all Earth rockets that follow you will be destroyed.

00:56:58.500 --> 00:56:59.420
Better do as he says.

00:56:59.580 --> 00:56:59.780
No.

00:57:00.000 --> 00:57:01.100
Let's make a dash back to the rocket.

00:57:01.440 --> 00:57:04.440
We can destroy your rocket before you reach it, Earthmen.

00:57:05.520 --> 00:57:06.500
Seems we have no choice.

00:57:07.710 --> 00:57:09.860
Very well, man of Venus, we're coming.

00:57:18.260 --> 00:57:19.400
Act it wisely, Earthmen.

00:57:20.310 --> 00:57:21.170
Let us kill them.

00:57:21.540 --> 00:57:22.640
Why waste time talking?

00:57:23.120 --> 00:57:24.620
You are too hasty, Cullis.

00:57:25.490 --> 00:57:27.910
First let us see what these Earthmen have to say for themselves.

00:57:28.300 --> 00:57:28.960
And their rocket?

00:57:29.190 --> 00:57:29.970
That will be taken care of.

00:57:30.960 --> 00:57:33.680
Alpha, enter the Earthman's rocket.

00:57:34.480 --> 00:57:37.200
See that no one touches the controls or uses the radio.

00:57:37.700 --> 00:57:37.880
Go.

00:57:39.370 --> 00:57:41.240
But is this really necessary?

00:57:42.090 --> 00:57:43.530
These men may come in peace.

00:57:43.930 --> 00:57:45.710
Perhaps it is a scientific expedition.

00:57:46.210 --> 00:57:47.850
They may come in the name of science,

00:57:47.850 --> 00:57:49.710
but kill in the name of conquest.

00:57:49.990 --> 00:57:51.560
No, we should kill them first.

00:57:51.680 --> 00:57:53.240
Silence, both of you.

00:57:54.230 --> 00:57:56.730
While I am master of Venus, you shall do as I say.

00:57:57.700 --> 00:57:59.360
Emos, go and receive our visitors.

00:58:10.140 --> 00:58:12.090
too late. Repeat, too late.

00:58:12.370 --> 00:58:14.430
The others have left the rocket and they've disappeared.

00:58:22.320 --> 00:58:23.860
Jim said it was a machine and that was

00:58:23.860 --> 00:58:26.190
the last I heard of him. Just a minute

00:58:26.190 --> 00:58:27.290
and I'll have another look out.

00:58:32.780 --> 00:58:34.250
No, there's no...

00:58:36.000 --> 00:58:36.620
Wait a minute.

00:58:37.680 --> 00:58:38.700
It's so misty.

00:58:38.760 --> 00:58:40.080
I thought I saw someone.

00:58:42.250 --> 00:58:44.020
Yes, someone coming.

00:58:47.480 --> 00:58:49.220
Yes, someone is coming.

00:58:49.440 --> 00:58:52.050
I can't see who it is yet.

00:58:52.480 --> 00:58:53.620
He's too far away.

00:58:53.800 --> 00:58:56.760
I still can't.

00:58:57.540 --> 00:58:59.980
Yes, I can see who it...

00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:00.400
What is that?

00:59:04.490 --> 00:59:05.210
What's happened?

00:59:06.290 --> 00:59:06.790
What?

00:59:17.480 --> 00:59:19.770
Control calling a start.

00:59:20.450 --> 00:59:21.530
Control calling a start.

00:59:22.250 --> 00:59:22.610
I hear you.

00:59:33.540 --> 00:59:54.890
What is the creature which threatens Pat in the Astarte Cabin?

00:59:55.790 --> 00:59:59.820
Find out in next week's episode, Prisoners of Venus.

01:00:21.920 --> 01:00:26.480
Unaware that the people of Venus are hostile and that Dr. Ballantyne has tried to stop them landing,

01:00:27.220 --> 01:00:29.960
Jim has released Mike and Peter from the gravity machine.

01:00:30.470 --> 01:00:34.870
In the underground city, the master of Venus awaits the arrival of the Earthmen.

01:00:35.210 --> 01:00:40.290
In the cabin of the rocket, Pat is petrified as she hears the robot Alpha climbing the ladder.

01:00:41.560 --> 01:00:45.500
Pete and Mike make their way cautiously through the secret tunnel.

01:00:48.150 --> 01:00:49.390
Seems to be as far as we can go.

01:00:49.760 --> 01:00:51.620
I wish we had a chance to tell Pat what was happening.

01:01:01.950 --> 01:01:02.110
Thank you.

01:01:31.280 --> 01:01:31.880
Where are we?

01:01:32.670 --> 01:01:33.530
Some kind of airlock.

01:01:34.380 --> 01:01:35.460
Can't you feel the pressure decreasing?

01:01:36.360 --> 01:01:37.720
Must be pumping the atmosphere out.

01:01:38.340 --> 01:01:38.720
You're right.

01:01:39.900 --> 01:01:41.260
And now they're pumping something else in.

01:01:42.510 --> 01:01:43.310
Let's hope it's air.

01:01:44.670 --> 01:01:44.950
Yes.

01:01:45.690 --> 01:01:46.090
Oxygen.

01:01:46.400 --> 01:01:47.360
We can take our masks off.

01:01:48.840 --> 01:01:49.840
It's hot in here.

01:01:50.490 --> 01:01:50.810
Oxygen.

01:01:51.860 --> 01:01:55.020
So that means the Venusians breathe the same sort of stuff as we breathe on Earth.

01:01:55.690 --> 01:01:58.610
Yes, but that man on the surface, he wasn't wearing any equipment.

01:01:58.830 --> 01:01:59.950
What was he breathing?

01:02:00.960 --> 01:02:02.060
It wasn't man on the citizen.

01:02:33.960 --> 01:02:37.190
Hello, Pat. Are you all right? Come in, please, Pat.

01:02:37.980 --> 01:02:52.560
Help me.

01:03:05.080 --> 01:03:07.620
Welcome. Welcome to Venus, Earthman.

01:03:08.530 --> 01:03:08.990
Who are you?

01:03:09.850 --> 01:03:10.850
My name is Imos.

01:03:11.770 --> 01:03:14.730
There is no reason to be afraid. I am human like yourselves.

01:03:15.560 --> 01:03:18.820
Our forefathers came from Earth, oh, many, many centuries ago.

01:03:19.400 --> 01:03:20.240
I don't understand.

01:03:20.500 --> 01:03:21.540
That will be explained.

01:03:22.250 --> 01:03:25.730
Enough for the moment to say that your ancestors drove us from the Earth.

01:03:25.990 --> 01:03:26.850
They settled here.

01:03:27.390 --> 01:03:28.490
We drove you from the Earth?

01:03:28.670 --> 01:03:29.070
Yes.

01:03:29.590 --> 01:03:29.970
Oh, it was...

01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:35.680
a long time ago it is true that there are still some venusians who hate and fear the earth people

01:03:35.680 --> 01:03:42.900
but i do not and i repeat you are welcome thank you from the voice we heard over the radio we

01:03:42.900 --> 01:03:48.840
were beginning to wonder if we were now that was voten our leader he is suspicious you must convince

01:03:48.840 --> 01:03:54.870
him that you come in peace unfortunately there are many here who believe that your rocket is

01:03:54.870 --> 01:03:59.910
the spearhead of an armed invasion oh but that's nonsense yes that is what i have told

01:04:01.120 --> 01:04:02.460
But you must be an earth boy.

01:04:03.340 --> 01:04:04.980
You know I have a son about your age.

01:04:05.220 --> 01:04:06.100
And a daughter too.

01:04:06.910 --> 01:04:08.910
Come, Lord Wotan must not be kept waiting.

01:04:09.550 --> 01:04:12.300
Strange, the sun seems to be shining down here.

01:04:12.520 --> 01:04:14.820
We have concealed sun filters on the surface.

01:04:15.100 --> 01:04:17.740
They catch the beneficial rays and pass them down to us.

01:04:18.170 --> 01:04:19.210
You mean you make your own weather?

01:04:19.330 --> 01:04:19.570
Yes.

01:04:20.010 --> 01:04:20.970
Is this tree real?

01:04:21.880 --> 01:04:22.700
Oh, yes.

01:04:23.330 --> 01:04:27.150
Of course, it took us a long time to grieve plants that can be grown in these artificial conditions.

01:04:27.510 --> 01:04:29.980
Even the soil, like the air we breathe, has...

01:04:30.000 --> 01:04:35.280
to be manufactured in our laboratories it's fantastic what i'd really like enough lord

01:04:35.360 --> 01:04:46.110
wotan is eager to meet you you may remove your helmets emos is a fool my lord if he has his way

01:04:46.110 --> 01:04:51.670
this earth spice will take back all our secrets then the earth people will come again to destroy

01:04:51.670 --> 01:04:57.000
us patient scholars at least we will question these people before we condemn them but why

01:04:57.000 --> 01:04:59.880
waste time they should be treated as enemy spice

01:05:00.000 --> 01:05:01.580
Because that's exactly what they are.

01:05:01.660 --> 01:05:02.400
Quiet, here they come.

01:05:08.760 --> 01:05:09.580
Earthmen, my lord.

01:05:09.720 --> 01:05:11.880
What is your name, Earthmen?

01:05:12.730 --> 01:05:15.620
Mike Riley, Jim Ballantyne, and I'm Peter Ross.

01:05:16.060 --> 01:05:18.260
You're speaking to Lord Burton, Master of Venus.

01:05:18.910 --> 01:05:21.190
This is Emus, Master of the Men of Skill.

01:05:21.690 --> 01:05:24.520
And I am Callus, Master of the Men of Action.

01:05:25.110 --> 01:05:25.630
Men of Action?

01:05:26.180 --> 01:05:28.340
So it was your people that tried to destroy our rocket.

01:05:28.640 --> 01:05:29.970
Yes, and you killed them.

01:05:30.350 --> 01:05:32.310
No, the death was accidental. It was their fault.

01:05:32.430 --> 01:05:34.130
We'd been wondering how they got to Earth.

01:05:34.570 --> 01:05:37.680
They travelled in what I believe you call a flying saucer.

01:05:38.170 --> 01:05:39.350
So this is where they come from.

01:05:39.970 --> 01:05:41.850
How do you know so much about life on Earth?

01:05:42.030 --> 01:05:43.590
Yes, and how is it you all speak English?

01:05:44.350 --> 01:05:46.930
We can receive your radio and television transmission.

01:05:50.120 --> 01:05:52.200
A new atomic weapon was exploded yesterday morning.

01:05:52.790 --> 01:05:55.290
It was a low-yield device of some four megatons

01:05:55.290 --> 01:05:59.100
and is described as having produced no radioactive fallout.

01:06:01.600 --> 01:06:03.020
That is a program from Earth.

01:06:03.890 --> 01:06:07.670
You see, on Earth you are always fighting, or getting ready to fight.

01:06:07.870 --> 01:06:10.730
Rioting took place in the streets and continued for several hours.

01:06:11.140 --> 01:06:14.500
Troops were called out to assist police, and tear gas was used.

01:06:16.140 --> 01:06:17.660
Don't change, you Earth people.

01:06:18.380 --> 01:06:20.640
You attack anyone who's different from yourselves.

01:06:21.250 --> 01:06:25.740
Oh, it may be the color of his skin, or the shape of his nose, or the god he believes in.

01:06:25.940 --> 01:06:27.960
If it's different, you turn on him like a beast.

01:06:28.080 --> 01:06:29.250
Please, that will do.

01:06:30.320 --> 01:06:31.120
You may sit down.

01:06:32.230 --> 01:06:33.250
Bring food and drink.

01:06:52.400 --> 01:06:56.100
Regret, you will have to remain in quarantine during your stay with us.

01:06:56.620 --> 01:06:57.020
Quarantine?

01:06:58.290 --> 01:06:58.830
Oh, yes.

01:06:59.660 --> 01:06:59.960
You may...

01:07:00.000 --> 01:07:06.150
brought germs from earth our people have no immunity so i'm afraid you will not be allowed

01:07:06.150 --> 01:07:12.840
to mix with the rest of the population what about yourselves emos colors and i have taken protective

01:07:12.840 --> 01:07:20.530
serum it was not possible to inoculate everyone in time everyone oh yes there are great cities

01:07:20.530 --> 01:07:27.300
beneath the surface of our planet this is just the threshold to our cap it was no accident

01:07:27.300 --> 01:07:29.860
that the gravity machine drew you to this spot.

01:07:30.000 --> 01:07:34.380
But it's Epsilon.

01:07:34.830 --> 01:07:35.230
Epsilon?

01:07:37.390 --> 01:07:38.170
He lasted well.

01:07:38.800 --> 01:07:39.920
You know, my father made him.

01:07:42.320 --> 01:07:44.060
Laboratory, take Epsilon out of circuit.

01:07:44.180 --> 01:07:44.800
There's been a fault.

01:07:46.190 --> 01:07:46.750
Made him?

01:07:48.920 --> 01:07:52.140
The work in our underground factories is unpleasant and dangerous.

01:07:52.820 --> 01:07:55.080
There are many jobs, too, which have to be done on the surface.

01:07:55.420 --> 01:07:56.880
Human beings are quite unsuitable.

01:08:05.820 --> 01:08:07.320
Yes. Burned out, I'm afraid.

01:08:08.300 --> 01:08:09.200
Gamma Omega, come here.

01:08:10.020 --> 01:08:12.400
I want you to take Epsilon to the laboratory.

01:08:13.170 --> 01:08:13.410
Quickly.

01:08:13.870 --> 01:08:15.270
Then return here.

01:08:17.530 --> 01:08:20.630
They have electronic brains in which is stored a small vocabulary

01:08:20.630 --> 01:08:22.430
so they can receive and obey orders.

01:08:22.690 --> 01:08:23.990
But if one breaks down,

01:08:24.180 --> 01:08:26.060
it is essential to remove it from the circuit

01:08:26.060 --> 01:08:27.160
or the others are affected.

01:08:29.010 --> 01:08:29.970
We had the Earthman were here.

01:08:30.000 --> 01:08:35.510
can we? Did you really come from Earth in a rocket? That's right. But you're no different

01:08:35.510 --> 01:08:41.080
from us, except that you've only got five fingers. Oh, how horrible. Mara, how rude.

01:08:42.130 --> 01:08:45.980
Apologize for my daughter, Earthman. That's all right. We must get used to being things from

01:08:45.980 --> 01:08:50.560
outer space. What are you doing here, children? You know very well this part of the city is

01:08:50.560 --> 01:08:55.090
isolated. I'm sorry, Father, but we just wanted to... Well, now you are here, you will have to stay.

01:08:55.550 --> 01:08:59.670
You are in quarantine, too. I wish to have a serious discussion with the Earthman.

01:09:00.700 --> 01:09:05.020
Thomas, Mara, take the earth boy to the isolation ward and stay with him.

01:09:05.950 --> 01:09:07.110
Please don't disturb us again.

01:09:08.600 --> 01:09:10.330
Yes, Lord Votan. This way.

01:09:10.890 --> 01:09:20.740
Let's make ourselves comfortable. The servitors will take your equipment.

01:09:21.240 --> 01:09:22.020
Lord Votan.

01:09:22.320 --> 01:09:23.020
Hand it over.

01:09:25.950 --> 01:09:29.860
I'm afraid it's only a cell, really. It was cleaned and turned into a quarantine room.

01:09:30.000 --> 01:09:34.550
they knew you were coming why does everybody treat us like their enemies father doesn't but

01:09:34.640 --> 01:09:39.660
after all your people did once drive our people away now he said that before but what does it

01:09:39.660 --> 01:09:46.380
mean don't you know about atlantis well i know the legend that once there was another continent

01:09:46.380 --> 01:09:51.300
on earth called atlantis but it was supposed to have disappeared beneath the sea thousands of

01:09:51.300 --> 01:09:55.960
years ago oh it's not a legend it's true and there were two sorts of people in atlantis

01:09:55.960 --> 01:09:59.890
some with five fingers like you some with six fingers like us and the six-fingered

01:10:00.000 --> 01:10:16.250
were the cleverest and became leaders those chaps give me the creeps do they of course we are used

01:10:16.250 --> 01:10:27.570
to them and before the end the scientists of atlantis were far ahead of any you've got today

01:10:27.570 --> 01:10:29.970
what happened then the five-fingered

01:10:30.000 --> 01:10:35.310
ones were jealous. They rose against our people. Soon it was more than your life was worth to have

01:10:35.310 --> 01:10:39.990
six fingers. So those that were left escaped. They made a spaceship in secret and came here

01:10:39.990 --> 01:10:44.740
to Venus. But we can't ever forget how your people treated us. Oh, but that was a long time

01:10:44.740 --> 01:10:51.000
ago. People have changed since then. I mean, do you hate me for having five fingers? Of course not.

01:10:54.730 --> 01:10:58.030
Horace, Horace, come with me. You'll wait here.

01:11:00.280 --> 01:11:02.560
Goodbye for the moment. I'm sure we're going to be friends.

01:11:02.740 --> 01:11:05.280
So am I. And I'm sorry I was rude about your fingers.

01:11:05.460 --> 01:11:07.680
That's all right. It's just a question of what you're used to.

01:11:07.940 --> 01:11:16.800
Come on. Relation room. It's more like a cell to me.

01:11:17.760 --> 01:11:18.920
Look, Mike, we've got to get away from here.

01:11:19.080 --> 01:11:20.360
Yes, but they seem so friendly.

01:11:20.890 --> 01:11:22.810
Kids are all right. And their father.

01:11:23.340 --> 01:11:25.960
That's for Votan and Callie. I shouldn't like to look at them one little bit.

01:11:26.080 --> 01:11:28.480
They've been trying to find out how the rocket works. I'm sure they want to steal it.

01:11:28.640 --> 01:11:29.880
Let's get back and blast off quickly.

01:11:30.280 --> 01:11:32.520
It's easier said than done. They've taken our oxygen masks.

01:11:32.720 --> 01:11:33.840
Well, let's ask for them back.

01:11:34.880 --> 01:11:35.220
Hey!

01:11:36.170 --> 01:11:36.570
Prisoners!

01:11:37.640 --> 01:11:40.380
But they are our guests. This is no way to treat them.

01:11:40.640 --> 01:11:43.360
You let them go back and tell Earth all about us, I suppose.

01:11:43.760 --> 01:11:46.870
And why not an exchange of scientific...

01:11:46.870 --> 01:11:48.890
Exchange of sentimental poppycock.

01:11:49.660 --> 01:11:51.480
Earth's next move would be to attack us.

01:11:51.840 --> 01:11:55.060
No, they must stay locked up till we learn how to fly their rocket.

01:11:55.520 --> 01:11:56.180
And then...

01:11:56.180 --> 01:11:58.320
Then we attack Earth in their own rocket.

01:11:58.820 --> 01:11:59.980
Attack is the best form of...

01:12:00.000 --> 01:12:02.080
defence. Suppose they will not tell you

01:12:02.080 --> 01:12:04.120
the secret of their rocket. There are ways

01:12:04.120 --> 01:12:06.870
of making them tell. No, no, this

01:12:06.870 --> 01:12:09.120
is all wrong. Lord Vogt and the Earthmen

01:12:09.120 --> 01:12:10.920
trust us. Let us trust

01:12:10.920 --> 01:12:12.880
them and live in peace with Earth.

01:12:13.280 --> 01:12:15.080
Cannot trust the five-fingered ones, my lord.

01:12:15.540 --> 01:12:17.520
They drove our ancestors from the face

01:12:17.520 --> 01:12:19.940
of the Earth, and unless we protect ourselves,

01:12:20.240 --> 01:12:21.740
their descendants will drive

01:12:21.740 --> 01:12:25.550
us from Venus. Alice is right.

01:12:26.060 --> 01:12:29.510
It shall be as he says. Will you

01:12:29.510 --> 01:12:29.970
come and let us...

01:12:30.000 --> 01:12:30.440
Get us out!

01:12:32.250 --> 01:12:33.190
It's no use.

01:12:33.270 --> 01:12:34.650
If there's anybody there, they aren't answering.

01:12:34.850 --> 01:12:35.650
What do we do?

01:12:35.870 --> 01:12:36.730
What can we do?

01:12:37.160 --> 01:12:38.580
Someone's bound to come along sooner or later.

01:12:38.990 --> 01:12:40.210
When they do, perhaps we make a break for it.

01:12:40.400 --> 01:12:40.680
Hey.

01:12:41.480 --> 01:12:41.900
Who's that?

01:12:42.100 --> 01:12:42.580
It's me.

01:12:42.880 --> 01:12:43.620
Behind the curtain.

01:12:46.710 --> 01:12:47.720
It's Wallace!

01:12:49.080 --> 01:12:49.460
Follow me.

01:12:49.520 --> 01:12:58.050
It escaped this way.

01:12:58.310 --> 01:12:58.870
What is it?

01:12:58.990 --> 01:12:59.650
The air shot.

01:13:00.570 --> 01:13:01.810
Quick, there's somebody coming. Go on, Jim.

01:13:19.900 --> 01:13:22.620
Together you'll get lost. There are hundreds of these air shafts.

01:13:22.940 --> 01:13:24.120
They're the passengers of the whole city.

01:13:24.240 --> 01:13:24.760
Where are we going?

01:13:24.900 --> 01:13:26.980
To the airlock. You must get back to your rocket and escape.

01:13:27.180 --> 01:13:28.500
But we haven't got our breathing equipment.

01:13:28.740 --> 01:13:29.520
We know what it is.

01:13:30.000 --> 01:13:33.820
They've escaped.

01:13:34.790 --> 01:13:35.050
What?

01:13:36.420 --> 01:13:36.940
Splendid.

01:13:38.240 --> 01:13:39.200
You'll regret that.

01:13:40.580 --> 01:13:43.470
Control, alert all servitors to capture the Earthmen.

01:13:44.080 --> 01:13:45.380
I want them alive.

01:13:46.020 --> 01:13:51.440
Yes, warning all servitors to be at large of the city.

01:13:52.060 --> 01:13:55.290
Get away, you'll see.

01:13:55.730 --> 01:13:56.490
Then you'll be sorry.

01:13:58.280 --> 01:13:59.300
Can't you say something?

01:14:02.840 --> 01:14:11.590
You're not a man at all. You're a machine soon fix you

01:15:07.920 --> 01:15:08.540
Ike!

01:15:11.150 --> 01:15:11.530
Boys!

01:15:23.240 --> 01:15:24.880
I'm afraid so.

01:15:25.250 --> 01:15:26.310
They may never get out.

01:15:33.140 --> 01:15:44.120
How will Peter escape from Callus and rejoin his friends?

01:15:45.550 --> 01:15:47.610
See episode six next week.

01:16:10.200 --> 01:16:15.240
Borlas, the friendly Venusian children, hear Callas plotting to invade the Earth using Astarte.

01:16:16.100 --> 01:16:18.540
And they release Peter, Mike and Jim from the cell.

01:16:19.640 --> 01:16:22.160
But they all get lost in the maze of underground tunnels.

01:16:34.760 --> 01:16:36.540
Just enough to stun him for a few minutes.

01:16:36.780 --> 01:16:38.140
Lock him up before he recovers.

01:16:38.340 --> 01:16:47.020
Is it that end?

01:16:47.400 --> 01:16:48.080
No, it isn't.

01:16:48.720 --> 01:16:51.910
We found the secret door when we were playing down here once.

01:16:52.090 --> 01:16:53.150
We never told us so.

01:16:53.350 --> 01:16:53.990
Follow me quickly.

01:16:57.430 --> 01:16:58.410
What is this place?

01:16:58.570 --> 01:16:59.970
It's where they keep the surface suits and...

01:17:00.000 --> 01:17:06.120
oxygen masks. They probably put yours here. Are these the ones? Yes. Thank goodness. I'll take a look

01:17:06.120 --> 01:17:25.380
outside to see if it's all clear. It's only me. You scared me. Where's Peter? I thought he was with you. We

01:17:25.380 --> 01:17:26.200
thought he was with you.

01:17:30.350 --> 01:17:32.340
Quite calm, quite relaxed.

01:17:32.960 --> 01:17:33.900
It is very peaceful.

01:17:34.930 --> 01:17:37.110
You are tired, very, very tired.

01:17:37.760 --> 01:17:40.140
You are tired, aren't you, Peter Ross?

01:17:40.490 --> 01:17:42.320
Yes, I am tired.

01:17:42.830 --> 01:17:43.970
You will sleep now.

01:17:44.540 --> 01:17:45.970
Sleep, sleep.

01:17:46.880 --> 01:17:47.900
You are asleep.

01:17:48.920 --> 01:17:50.770
Yes, I am asleep.

01:17:51.280 --> 01:17:52.320
You can hear me.

01:17:53.080 --> 01:17:54.790
Yes, I can hear you.

01:17:55.120 --> 01:17:57.260
You will answer all my questions now.

01:17:57.910 --> 01:17:59.790
I will answer all your questions.

01:18:00.570 --> 01:18:03.290
Omega, microphone, switch.

01:18:05.760 --> 01:18:07.280
What fuel is your rocket?

01:18:08.530 --> 01:18:11.290
Mixture of AX2 and LC3.

01:18:11.920 --> 01:18:13.480
How is the mixture controlled?

01:18:14.420 --> 01:18:21.270
On a panel to the left of the pilot, there is a lever controlling four pairs of valves operated on the throttle principle.

01:18:22.280 --> 01:18:29.980
By a system of electrically operated shutter relays, the flow of AX2 itself acts as the main governor controlling the rate of L...

01:18:30.780 --> 01:18:33.170
You don't know what I'm doing, do you?

01:18:33.870 --> 01:18:35.070
No, of course you don't.

01:18:35.210 --> 01:18:37.770
You're just a tin can with a lot of wires inside.

01:18:39.120 --> 01:18:43.300
Well, I'm going to take this fire extinguisher like this

01:18:43.300 --> 01:18:46.100
and show you something very interesting.

01:18:47.020 --> 01:18:48.560
You're not going without your friend, are you?

01:18:48.800 --> 01:18:51.400
No, we'll take his stuff ready to make a dash for it when we find him.

01:18:51.680 --> 01:18:52.880
Come on, come on.

01:18:53.170 --> 01:18:53.490
What's that?

01:18:55.560 --> 01:18:55.860
Listen.

01:19:00.670 --> 01:19:01.170
What's happening?

01:19:01.740 --> 01:19:02.460
You'll find out.

01:19:16.780 --> 01:19:18.340
They locked your friend in one of the old dungeons.

01:19:18.810 --> 01:19:19.590
Do you think we can get him out?

01:19:20.000 --> 01:19:20.880
There's a guard outside.

01:19:21.140 --> 01:19:21.560
Only one?

01:19:21.720 --> 01:19:22.160
Let's see.

01:19:32.620 --> 01:19:34.540
If I make a dash, that guard's sure to follow me.

01:19:34.860 --> 01:19:36.420
So as he comes past the door, you hit him.

01:19:36.560 --> 01:19:37.340
Fine, but you're forgetting.

01:19:37.500 --> 01:19:38.800
He'll have one of those paralyser guns.

01:19:39.000 --> 01:19:39.560
It's all right.

01:19:39.760 --> 01:19:41.720
They only knock you out if the light strikes in your eyes.

01:19:41.880 --> 01:19:42.400
What about the noise?

01:19:42.560 --> 01:19:44.360
It's unpleasant, but it won't work on its own.

01:19:44.760 --> 01:19:45.820
In that case, here I go.

01:19:46.400 --> 01:19:46.940
Ready, Mike?

01:19:54.460 --> 01:19:54.780
Aye!

01:20:01.690 --> 01:20:03.180
Hey, see these bells?

01:20:04.230 --> 01:20:04.810
There they are.

01:20:07.950 --> 01:20:08.450
Well done, Borna.

01:20:09.010 --> 01:20:10.050
Let's get rid of this joker.

01:20:10.570 --> 01:20:11.070
Come on.

01:20:15.870 --> 01:20:21.420
Which way to the airlock?

01:20:21.600 --> 01:20:22.000
This way.

01:20:29.180 --> 01:20:29.940
Well done, Borna.

01:20:30.410 --> 01:20:32.920
Well done, Mara. You've rounded them all up.

01:20:33.880 --> 01:20:36.920
These are only effective against humans, not against servitors.

01:20:37.180 --> 01:20:39.420
Thanks for telling me. Next time I'll get you.

01:20:39.680 --> 01:20:41.040
There won't be a next time for you.

01:20:48.840 --> 01:20:50.660
You see, if I bang this knob...

01:20:51.040 --> 01:20:54.900
Calling all servitors. The Earthmen have been recaptured.

01:20:55.250 --> 01:20:57.350
You haven't won yet. Here goes.

01:21:06.640 --> 01:21:08.140
servitor control calling

01:21:08.420 --> 01:21:10.660
getting distress signals from alpha

01:21:10.660 --> 01:21:11.860
he's overloading

01:21:11.860 --> 01:21:13.830
is that the servitor in the earth rocket

01:21:13.890 --> 01:21:15.430
yes Lord Bolton

01:21:15.430 --> 01:21:17.150
shall I take him out of circuit

01:21:17.150 --> 01:21:19.320
not yet the rocket must be guarded

01:21:19.320 --> 01:21:21.700
send in another servitor to relieve him

01:21:22.140 --> 01:21:23.760
as you say Lord Bolton

01:21:34.800 --> 01:21:43.200
O'Reilly, the Supreme Council of Venus found you guilty of spying and of planning an armed

01:21:43.200 --> 01:21:49.140
invasion. A penalty for such crimes is death. There's been no trial. We've had no chance to

01:21:49.140 --> 01:21:54.860
defend ourselves. There is no argument with the Supreme Council. There is no appeal against its

01:21:54.860 --> 01:21:59.580
decisions. Fine justice for a so-called advanced civilization. But don't you know what this will

01:21:59.580 --> 01:21:59.820
mean?

01:22:00.190 --> 01:22:01.350
War between our planets.

01:22:01.830 --> 01:22:03.830
Emos, can't you make them understand that?

01:22:04.070 --> 01:22:10.780
I have tried. Lord Votan, if you cannot be merciful, be sensible.

01:22:11.450 --> 01:22:12.610
Think what a war will mean.

01:22:13.680 --> 01:22:15.720
The Supreme Council have made their decisions.

01:22:15.840 --> 01:22:20.760
We have a humane and simple way of dealing with enemies of the state.

01:22:21.580 --> 01:22:23.400
No violence, no bloodshed.

01:22:24.300 --> 01:22:26.540
You will be escorted to the surface and left there,

01:22:27.270 --> 01:22:29.170
without oxygen masks, of course.

01:22:29.600 --> 01:22:29.980
Take them off.

01:22:30.000 --> 01:22:41.540
stop and buy and see you murder these innocent people the sentence of the

01:22:41.540 --> 01:22:43.240
supreme council be carried out

01:23:00.250 --> 01:23:01.110
I'll see you next time.

01:23:30.760 --> 01:23:31.420
Hey.

01:23:34.940 --> 01:23:35.280
Emergency.

01:23:38.040 --> 01:23:39.880
Servitors in the circuit have collapsed.

01:23:40.370 --> 01:23:41.710
The laboratory is on fire.

01:23:42.320 --> 01:23:42.620
Call us.

01:23:42.800 --> 01:23:43.180
Come quickly.

01:23:46.260 --> 01:23:47.120
Start you calling control.

01:23:47.300 --> 01:23:48.460
Start you calling control.

01:23:48.780 --> 01:23:49.540
Come in, please.

01:23:49.830 --> 01:23:50.150
Over.

01:23:52.200 --> 01:23:53.040
I don't understand it.

01:23:53.260 --> 01:23:55.320
Pat must have got the bed of her guard and just the whole circuit.

01:23:55.480 --> 01:23:56.160
Good old Pat.

01:23:56.810 --> 01:23:57.790
And all the time he...

01:23:57.840 --> 01:23:58.760
It was a robot.

01:23:59.160 --> 01:23:59.980
Anyway, it's done.

01:24:00.090 --> 01:24:02.840
for now. Quick, let's get our masks

01:24:02.840 --> 01:24:04.780
and get into the airlock. No, there's no time. Come on, this way.

01:24:07.230 --> 01:24:09.200
Well done, Pat, but we have to think of your

01:24:09.200 --> 01:24:11.080
safety now. I'll give you instructions

01:24:11.080 --> 01:24:13.080
for setting course to return on your own.

01:24:13.780 --> 01:24:15.870
Oh, no, I can't leave yet. I'm sure

01:24:15.870 --> 01:24:17.970
they'll get away. Please give them more time.

01:24:19.100 --> 01:24:20.100
There's no one in here. Come on.

01:24:30.600 --> 01:24:34.620
the same as the kids in the isolation so maybe they know how to bring him round good idea right

01:24:39.450 --> 01:24:46.870
pat we'll give them 30 minutes but after that you must come back 30 minutes starting now

01:24:47.340 --> 01:24:57.080
don't suppose we'll ever see them again

01:25:00.120 --> 01:25:00.380
Jim!

01:25:00.810 --> 01:25:01.790
Father, what happened?

01:25:02.110 --> 01:25:03.390
He's coming round, I think.

01:25:03.710 --> 01:25:04.190
Murder.

01:25:04.850 --> 01:25:06.370
I won't stand for murder.

01:25:08.960 --> 01:25:11.120
Callas and Wotan, they are raving madmen.

01:25:12.000 --> 01:25:13.060
You've got to stop them.

01:25:13.360 --> 01:25:14.100
Stop them from what?

01:25:14.690 --> 01:25:16.930
Destroying all human life on the earth.

01:25:17.560 --> 01:25:21.880
Listen, accident byproducts of certain experiments we were making.

01:25:22.060 --> 01:25:24.300
We discovered a new deadly plague virus.

01:25:24.720 --> 01:25:27.300
Before it could be destroyed, Callas got hold of the formula

01:25:27.300 --> 01:25:29.980
and he forced my staff to manufacture large quantities of...

01:25:30.320 --> 01:25:31.720
And he plans to use it against Earth?

01:25:32.020 --> 01:25:36.140
Yes, to destroy mankind and leave the great return from Venus.

01:25:36.740 --> 01:25:39.400
I'd rather we stayed on Venus forever than went back like that.

01:25:39.850 --> 01:25:41.470
Where's this stuff kept? Can't we destroy it?

01:25:41.820 --> 01:25:44.200
The virus is hidden in a cave beyond the airlock.

01:25:44.640 --> 01:25:47.080
It is down a tunnel which can be entered only from the crater.

01:25:47.410 --> 01:25:48.070
You must go!

01:25:48.390 --> 01:25:49.750
Come on, we've no time to lose.

01:26:01.280 --> 01:26:08.550
Of course, they're still here. Get your breathing out, please.

01:26:09.380 --> 01:26:10.200
There's someone coming.

01:26:10.820 --> 01:26:12.300
Wait, Pony! Come on, Jim.

01:26:14.410 --> 01:26:29.980
The passengers, two that way.

01:26:30.000 --> 01:26:34.030
You two that way. Two of you stay here, and you two follow me to the airlock.

01:26:34.330 --> 01:26:36.090
They're about to try and get to their rockets sooner or later.

01:26:36.730 --> 01:26:36.970
Move!

01:26:42.550 --> 01:26:43.130
Two on it.

01:26:43.800 --> 01:26:44.280
They're coming.

01:26:51.320 --> 01:26:52.120
Go on the other way.

01:26:53.750 --> 01:26:54.850
How serious is the damage?

01:26:55.340 --> 01:26:58.540
Bad enough, my lord. Much of the virus has been destroyed by the fire.

01:26:59.020 --> 01:26:59.960
Equipment that makes it.

01:27:00.250 --> 01:27:04.110
And how, unfortunately, but it will take us 20 hours to make a new batch of virus.

01:27:04.310 --> 01:27:05.090
Waste no time, then.

01:27:05.510 --> 01:27:07.670
We're ready to launch our attack on Earth in their own rocket.

01:27:08.300 --> 01:27:09.860
Make sure the rest of the virus is ready.

01:27:10.120 --> 01:27:10.740
As you say, Michael.

01:27:12.920 --> 01:27:14.120
Let's search the laboratory.

01:27:26.420 --> 01:27:27.800
Excuse me, sir. We're looking for the Earthmen.

01:27:27.980 --> 01:27:29.960
They're not here, you fool. Go and look someone.

01:27:30.600 --> 01:27:31.120
Yes, sir.

01:27:42.710 --> 01:27:45.520
Tower calling a start day. Any sign of them yet, Pat?

01:27:50.420 --> 01:27:52.600
Party to control. No sign yet.

01:27:57.350 --> 01:27:58.790
20 minutes to blast off time, Pat.

01:27:59.680 --> 01:27:59.960
You'd better...

01:28:00.000 --> 01:28:04.740
start checking your instruments. You know the drill. Very well, but...

01:28:05.820 --> 01:28:09.180
Please Pat, no buts. You can't risk staying there much longer.

01:28:09.720 --> 01:28:13.300
There's no time to lose. We must attack with what virus we already have.

01:28:13.440 --> 01:28:16.660
But will it be enough? First surprise attack in their own rocket, yes.

01:28:17.360 --> 01:28:20.870
Then when they're stricken and disorganized, we can follow it up in our own spaceship.

01:28:22.480 --> 01:28:24.460
Hurry up, you two. Take that virus to the store.

01:28:24.640 --> 01:28:26.500
There's someone in the rocket. A girl.

01:28:26.660 --> 01:28:29.640
You won't just let us in. We'll force our way in.

01:28:30.000 --> 01:28:30.640
Damage the rocket?

01:28:31.030 --> 01:28:31.330
No.

01:28:32.020 --> 01:28:32.860
I've got a better idea.

01:28:33.420 --> 01:28:33.660
Listen.

01:28:40.740 --> 01:28:41.380
More virus.

01:28:42.360 --> 01:28:44.940
You know that filthy stuff's the other side of the airlock, the better I shall like it.

01:28:50.600 --> 01:28:50.980
Right, Jim?

01:28:51.160 --> 01:28:52.080
I think so.

01:28:52.360 --> 01:28:53.160
This is just the beginning.

01:28:53.420 --> 01:28:55.930
Get your mask, son.

01:28:56.300 --> 01:28:57.380
The oxygen's being pumped up.

01:29:03.720 --> 01:29:04.980
Carlos, come quickly!

01:29:18.720 --> 01:29:19.120
Surface?

01:29:20.980 --> 01:29:21.860
Leads to the virus cave.

01:29:23.310 --> 01:29:24.010
Hang the virus.

01:29:24.500 --> 01:29:26.480
Our first duty is to pat on the rocket.

01:29:26.740 --> 01:29:27.920
We've got to try and destroy it, Mike.

01:29:28.000 --> 01:29:29.220
Otherwise, Earth will never be safe.

01:29:29.660 --> 01:29:29.960
Peter's...

01:29:30.000 --> 01:29:32.660
Right. Destroy the virus first, then get back to the rocket.

01:29:34.680 --> 01:29:35.520
All right, you win.

01:29:48.250 --> 01:29:51.310
Nice little surprise for the Earth girl.

01:29:54.550 --> 01:29:57.090
What are Voten and Callas planning for that?

01:29:58.210 --> 01:29:59.970
Come next week and see episode...

01:30:00.000 --> 01:30:29.980
kill on sight. Once again, the Earthmen have been captured by Kallus. But just in time, Pat destroys our...

01:30:30.000 --> 01:30:32.230
and all the servitors collapse.

01:30:33.520 --> 01:30:36.200
Dr. Valentine tells Pat she must take off alone,

01:30:36.780 --> 01:30:38.900
but Pat pleads to wait for the others.

01:30:40.440 --> 01:30:40.840
Fools!

01:30:41.720 --> 01:30:42.120
Burgers!

01:30:42.990 --> 01:30:44.110
Call yourselves men of action?

01:30:44.840 --> 01:30:48.560
You let yourselves be outweated by two miserable Earthmen and a wretched boy.

01:30:49.320 --> 01:30:51.200
They must be stopped before reaching the rocket.

01:30:52.240 --> 01:30:53.400
I want every man on the surface.

01:30:53.920 --> 01:30:55.660
That rocket must not be allowed to blast off.

01:30:56.000 --> 01:30:56.840
Yes, Lord Callas.

01:30:57.030 --> 01:30:59.730
And if we should see the Earthmen, kill them on sight.

01:31:00.670 --> 01:31:05.000
You, you shall remain in custody till the Earthmen are defeated.

01:31:05.500 --> 01:31:06.960
Then we shall decide what to do with you.

01:31:07.590 --> 01:31:08.190
Take them away.

01:31:08.290 --> 01:31:10.800
Now wait, men of Venus.

01:31:11.570 --> 01:31:13.910
Votan and Kallus are leading you to destruction.

01:31:15.000 --> 01:31:16.980
Their madness will bring about a war with Earth,

01:31:17.020 --> 01:31:19.380
and that will mean the end of both planets.

01:31:20.130 --> 01:31:22.110
Rise against them before it is too late.

01:31:22.310 --> 01:31:22.730
Treason!

01:31:23.380 --> 01:31:26.170
You've sentenced yourself to death, and your children too.

01:31:27.670 --> 01:31:28.630
Children are innocent.

01:31:28.950 --> 01:31:29.970
You have infected them with...

01:31:30.000 --> 01:31:31.340
with your own dangerous ideas.

01:31:32.110 --> 01:31:33.590
You must all die, take them away!

01:31:36.030 --> 01:31:38.010
To the surface!

01:31:44.830 --> 01:31:47.170
Control calling Venus rocket Astarte.

01:31:47.490 --> 01:31:48.490
Are you receiving me?

01:31:48.780 --> 01:31:49.100
Over.

01:31:49.870 --> 01:31:52.110
Astarte, receiving you loud and clear.

01:31:52.460 --> 01:31:52.660
Over.

01:31:53.370 --> 01:31:54.430
Receiving you loud and clear.

01:31:54.780 --> 01:31:54.980
Over.

01:31:55.260 --> 01:31:56.360
Time's running short, Pat.

01:31:57.120 --> 01:31:59.880
Stand by to start your return to Earth in five minutes.

01:32:01.790 --> 01:32:03.550
But, Dad, I can't believe they're dead.

01:32:14.120 --> 01:32:16.120
Ah, grief.

01:32:16.240 --> 01:32:19.550
Must be enough here to wipe out the whole population of the Earth.

01:32:21.000 --> 01:32:21.800
How do we destroy it?

01:32:22.490 --> 01:32:24.110
The only way to kill a virus is burners.

01:32:24.440 --> 01:32:25.580
There's some incendiants in the rocket.

01:32:25.680 --> 01:32:26.140
They do it.

01:32:26.960 --> 01:32:27.320
It's true.

01:32:27.400 --> 01:32:27.900
I'll go and fetch them.

01:32:28.390 --> 01:32:28.970
No, let me.

01:32:29.320 --> 01:32:29.960
If you go on the...

01:32:30.000 --> 01:32:31.920
surface dressed like that Pat will take you for a Venusian

01:32:31.920 --> 01:32:34.620
but she'll recognize my suit. Do you know the way?

01:32:34.840 --> 01:32:36.480
Yes. Vultimus gave us clear directions.

01:32:36.920 --> 01:32:38.600
I can be up there within a moment. I'll off you go then.

01:32:45.800 --> 01:32:52.340
To the surface. You suspect

01:32:52.340 --> 01:32:54.980
nothing. So go straight to the rocket and remember

01:32:55.220 --> 01:32:57.140
your duty is to stop it blasting off.

01:32:57.320 --> 01:32:58.820
And if the girl resists Lord Callas.

01:32:59.280 --> 01:32:59.720
Kill her.

01:33:07.360 --> 01:33:07.960
Are you blind?

01:33:08.560 --> 01:33:11.420
